# Local compliance term list — never commit this file.
# It contains the client/employer names you are scanning *against*.
# Anchored at repo root so a skill asset can still be named this.
/compliance-terms.txt
*.local

# Private planning documents. These discuss employer context, IP boundaries and
# launch strategy — none of which belongs in a public repository. Keep them
# locally; they are the source material, not the product.
# Anchored at root on purpose: a bare `plan.md` also hides skill assets
# (e.g. ninety-day-onboarding/assets/plan.md).
/plan.md
/project-status.md
/01-github-profile-e-growth.md
/notes/

# Personal working notes. Not sensitive — local-testing.md is a maintainer
# runbook that contains absolute paths from this machine. If it ever gets
# generalised, it belongs in CONTRIBUTING.md rather than here.
/local-testing.md

# The E2E prompt library. Kept local on purpose: published trigger prompts
# stop being a fair test, because anyone tuning a description against them
# is optimising for the test set rather than for real users.
# The RULE that maintains it lives in AGENTS.md and IS committed, so any
# agent in any session recreates this file if it is missing.
/local-testing-scripts.md

# Local harness state. Matt's repo ignores `.claude` for the same reason:
# marketplace add / plugin install write project settings here.
# Do NOT ignore `.claude-plugin/` or `.codex-plugin/` — those are the
# public channel-B and channel-C manifests.
/.claude/
/.cursor/
/.codex/
skills-lock.json

# Secrets
.env
.env.*

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Node
node_modules/

# Scratch
scratch/
tmp/
*.log
